---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Website Services for Therapists | Brighter Sites"
  description="Custom website design, responsive development, launch support, analytics, and ongoing site care for therapy practices."
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Services</p>

      <h1>Everything your practice needs for a professional web presence.</h1>

      <p class="page-lead">
        Brighter Sites handles the design and technical work behind your
        website so you can stay focused on your practice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What we build</p>
        <h2>A complete website—not just a homepage.</h2>

        <p>
          Your site is planned around how prospective clients actually use it:
          learning about your practice, understanding your services, getting a
          feel for the clinician, and finding a clear next step.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature">
          <span class="feature-number">01</span>
          <h3>Custom website design</h3>
          <p>
            A visual system, layout, typography, and color palette developed
            around the personality of your practice.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <span class="feature-number">02</span>
          <h3>Responsive development</h3>
          <p>
            Pages built to work naturally across phones, tablets, laptops, and
            larger displays.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <span class="feature-number">03</span>
          <h3>Practice-focused pages</h3>
          <p>
            Services, clinician profiles, approaches, contact information, and
            other pages organized around the questions prospective clients ask.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <span class="feature-number">04</span>
          <h3>Search-ready structure</h3>
          <p>
            Clean page structure, metadata, readable URLs, sitemap support, and
            a technical foundation that search engines can understand.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <span class="feature-number">05</span>
          <h3>Analytics</h3>
          <p>
            Practical website analytics can help you understand which pages are
            being viewed and how visitors move through the site.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <span class="feature-number">06</span>
          <h3>Launch and ongoing care</h3>
          <p>
            Domain connection, deployment, technical launch, and future updates
            as your practice grows or changes.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="container service-detail-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built around real practice needs</p>
        <h2>We pay attention to the details clients notice.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="detail-list">
        <div>
          <h3>Clear navigation</h3>
          <p>
            Visitors should be able to understand where they are and find
            important information without hunting for it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Strong mobile experience</h3>
          <p>
            Contact buttons, menus, service information, and calls to action
            remain easy to use on a phone.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Thoughtful client pathways</h3>
          <p>
            We make it obvious how someone can learn more, request an
            appointment, or reach the appropriate client portal.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Performance and maintainability</h3>
          <p>
            Sites are built to remain fast, understandable, and practical to
            maintain rather than becoming increasingly complicated over time.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Have an existing site?</p>
        <h2>You do not necessarily need to start from zero.</h2>

        <p>
          We can also look at an existing therapy website and determine whether
          a focused redesign or a complete rebuild makes more sense.
        </p>

        <a class="button" href="/contact/">Talk about your site</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
